1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,202
Laddoo Lab now talks to customers
in three different ways.

2
00:00:04,502 --> 00:00:06,378
The pack says tiffin sweet.

3
00:00:06,378 --> 00:00:08,155
Dev's post says gym snack.

4
00:00:08,155 --> 00:00:10,288
Arjun calls it a festive treat.

5
00:00:10,838 --> 00:00:11,738
Mrs.

6
00:00:11,351 --> 00:00:14,605
Rao sees all three, and
remembers none of them.

7
00:00:14,605 --> 00:00:15,841
What went wrong?

8
00:00:16,491 --> 00:00:20,440
Zoya calls the team together to
plan their first real campaign.

9
00:00:20,790 --> 00:00:25,419
A campaign is a planned set of messages,
over a few weeks, with one goal.

10
00:00:25,769 --> 00:00:27,070
Her rule is simple.

11
00:00:27,070 --> 00:00:29,393
Every message must say the same thing.

12
00:00:30,043 --> 00:00:34,071
This idea is called integrated
marketing communications.

13
00:00:34,371 --> 00:00:39,565
Kotler and Armstrong describe it as
joining up all of a company's communication

14
00:00:39,565 --> 00:00:40,465
channels,

15
00:00:40,640 --> 00:00:44,767
to deliver a clear, consistent and
compelling message about the company

16
00:00:44,767 --> 00:00:45,978
and its products.

17
00:00:46,328 --> 00:00:51,751
In 1993, Don Schultz of Northwestern
University co-wrote the first textbook

18
00:00:51,751 --> 00:00:52,651
on it.

19
00:00:52,907 --> 00:00:55,553
In simple words: many channels, one voice.

20
00:00:56,203 --> 00:00:59,171
A brand has five main
tools to talk to people.

21
00:00:59,171 --> 00:01:01,584
Together, they are the promotion mix.

22
00:01:01,934 --> 00:01:02,910
Advertising.

23
00:01:02,910 --> 00:01:06,172
Paid messages, like a
poster or a video ad.

24
00:01:06,472 --> 00:01:07,632
Sales promotion.

25
00:01:07,632 --> 00:01:11,052
A short offer to buy now,
like a festive discount.

26
00:01:11,352 --> 00:01:12,538
Personal selling.

27
00:01:12,538 --> 00:01:15,948
A person talking to a
buyer, like Arjun at a shop.

28
00:01:16,248 --> 00:01:17,388
Public relations.

29
00:01:17,388 --> 00:01:20,471
Building a good name,
like a story in the news.

30
00:01:20,771 --> 00:01:22,880
And direct and digital marketing.

31
00:01:22,880 --> 00:01:26,542
Talking to people one to one,
like a message or a post.

32
00:01:27,192 --> 00:01:29,215
Now watch one week of Mrs.

33
00:01:29,215 --> 00:01:31,121
Rao's life, the old way.

34
00:01:31,471 --> 00:01:33,901
On Monday, she sees Dev's gym post.

35
00:01:33,901 --> 00:01:36,832
On Wednesday, a festive
poster at the shop.

36
00:01:37,182 --> 00:01:39,082
On Friday, the tiffin pack.

37
00:01:39,082 --> 00:01:41,077
Three messages that don't match.

38
00:01:41,427 --> 00:01:43,943
Her memory of Laddoo Lab stays weak.

39
00:01:43,943 --> 00:01:45,247
She buys nothing.

40
00:01:45,897 --> 00:01:48,404
Now the same week, the integrated way.

41
00:01:48,404 --> 00:01:50,855
One message: the healthy tiffin sweet.

42
00:01:51,205 --> 00:01:52,825
Monday, the post says it.

43
00:01:52,825 --> 00:01:54,921
Wednesday, the shop poster says it.

44
00:01:54,921 --> 00:01:56,541
Friday, the pack says it.

45
00:01:56,891 --> 00:01:59,062
Each time, her memory gets stronger.

46
00:01:59,412 --> 00:02:02,548
On Saturday, she buys a pack
for her daughter's tiffin.

47
00:02:03,198 --> 00:02:04,455
Many channels.

48
00:02:04,455 --> 00:02:05,478
One voice.

49
00:02:06,178 --> 00:02:08,831
Zoya plans the campaign in four steps.

50
00:02:08,831 --> 00:02:09,731
One.

51
00:02:09,358 --> 00:02:13,167
Know the audience: busy parents
who pack school tiffins.

52
00:02:13,517 --> 00:02:14,417
Two.

53
00:02:14,037 --> 00:02:15,138
Set the goal.

54
00:02:15,138 --> 00:02:18,970
Make a thousand parents aware
of Laddoo Lab in one month.

55
00:02:19,320 --> 00:02:20,220
Three.

56
00:02:19,893 --> 00:02:22,107
Write one message, with one look.

57
00:02:22,107 --> 00:02:24,649
Same words and same colours, everywhere.

58
00:02:24,999 --> 00:02:25,899
Four.

59
00:02:25,528 --> 00:02:28,680
Pick the tools, and check
the results every week.

60
00:02:29,330 --> 00:02:31,297
Where do we see this at work today?

61
00:02:31,647 --> 00:02:32,668
One message.

62
00:02:32,668 --> 00:02:37,681
A phone maker uses the same line on
TV, in its app and in its stores.

63
00:02:38,031 --> 00:02:38,931
One look.

64
00:02:38,847 --> 00:02:43,100
A bank uses the same colours on
its cards, branches and website.

65
00:02:43,450 --> 00:02:45,488
The right tool for each job.

66
00:02:45,488 --> 00:02:49,818
An airline uses ads to get noticed,
and app messages at check-in.

67
00:02:50,168 --> 00:02:51,407
Check the results.

68
00:02:51,407 --> 00:02:55,441
A food delivery app tries two
ads, and keeps the one that works.

69
00:02:56,091 --> 00:02:58,014
But is one voice always easy?

70
00:02:58,014 --> 00:02:58,914
No.

71
00:02:58,793 --> 00:02:59,842
The good side.

72
00:02:59,842 --> 00:03:02,934
People remember you, and
every rupee works harder.

73
00:03:03,284 --> 00:03:04,346
The hard side.

74
00:03:04,346 --> 00:03:08,161
Teams pull in different ways,
and one message can get boring.

75
00:03:08,511 --> 00:03:10,495
Dev wants a funny gym video.

76
00:03:10,495 --> 00:03:14,266
Zoya says yes, but only if
it ends with the tiffin box.

77
00:03:14,616 --> 00:03:19,114
So the video shows a dad at the gym,
packing laddoos for his son's tiffin.

78
00:03:19,464 --> 00:03:20,364
The lesson?

79
00:03:20,302 --> 00:03:23,263
Keep one voice, but find
fresh ways to say it.

80
00:03:23,913 --> 00:03:24,821
Quick check.

81
00:03:24,821 --> 00:03:28,443
The post, the poster and the
pack all say the same line.

82
00:03:28,443 --> 00:03:29,453
What is this?

83
00:03:31,353 --> 00:03:33,734
Integrated marketing communications!

84
00:03:33,734 --> 00:03:36,189
Many channels, one clear message.

85
00:03:36,789 --> 00:03:37,799
So, remember.

86
00:03:38,099 --> 00:03:42,591
Integrated marketing communications
means every channel sends one clear

87
00:03:42,591 --> 00:03:43,491
message.

88
00:03:43,711 --> 00:03:48,488
The promotion mix has five tools:
advertising, sales promotion, personal

89
00:03:48,488 --> 00:03:51,164
selling, public relations and digital.

90
00:03:51,514 --> 00:03:55,107
And plan it in order: audience,
goal, message, then tools.

91
00:03:55,707 --> 00:03:59,859
Next time: advertising, sales
promotion, and a festive offer.
